        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "performance",
        "title": "Concurrent thread count can exceed core count with many regions",
        "explanation": "All regions are now prefaulted at the same time, and every non-empty region gets at least one thread. The scale-down pass also keeps a floor of 1 per region (cmp::max(1, ...)). With more regions than cores, for example many zones plus virtio-mem regions on a small host, the total stays above machine_cores. The old 16-thread cap and the one-region-at-a-time behaviour are both gone, so the thread count is unbounded by core count.",
        "suggestion": "After scaling, enforce a hard cap. For example, fall back to processing regions in batches, or merge small regions into shared workers, so the total number of threads is at most machine_cores.",
        "evidence": "plan.threads = cmp::max(1, plan.threads * machine_cores / total);",
        "confidence": 0.55,
        "id": "665a85690d30",
        "hunk_id": "vmm/src/prefault.rs#2",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "vmm/src/prefault.rs",
        "start_line": 255,
        "end_line": 258,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "test",
        "title": "Test assumes NUMA node0 sysfs exists on the build host",
        "explanation": "Kernels built without CONFIG_NUMA, and some containers or sandboxes, do not expose /sys/devices/system/node/node0/cpulist. On those hosts numa_node_cpu_set(0) returns None and the unwrap panics, so the unit test fails.",
        "suggestion": "Skip the test when the sysfs file does not exist, rather than unwrapping.",
        "evidence": "let (cpu_set, count) = numa_node_cpu_set(0).unwrap();",
